              "text": "You cannot legally buy a live Japanese dwarf flying squirrel (*Pteromys momonga*), also known as the *momonga*, as a pet if you live outside of Japan. \n\n### Why You Cannot Buy One\n* **Strict Export Laws:** The Japanese dwarf flying squirrel is endemic to the forests of Japan (specifically the Honshu, Shikoku, and Kyushu islands). Japan has highly restrictive wildlife protection laws that prohibit the capture, commercial trade, and export of its native species for the pet trade.\n* **No Captive Breeding Programs:** There are no legal, established captive-breeding populations of *Pteromys momonga* anywhere in North America, Europe, or other regions.\n* **Online Scams:** Because of their viral internet cuteness, some sketchy \"exotic pet\" websites may claim to have Japanese dwarf flying squirrels for sale. **These are almost always scams** designed to steal your money, or they are highly illegal wildlife smuggling operations. \n\n### Great Legal and Ethical Alternatives\nIf you are looking for an incredibly cute, gliding pocket pet, there are ethical, captive-bred options available depending on your local laws:\n\n1. **Southern Flying Squirrel (*Glaucomys volans*):** \n   * **The Closest Alternative:** Native to North America, these squirrels look remarkably similar to their Japanese counterparts, with big dark eyes and incredibly soft fur. \n   * **Availability:** They are legal to keep as pets in many U.S. states. Because they are bred domestically, you can purchase them legally from reputable, USDA-licensed breeders (such as Janda Exotic Animal Ranch in Texas).\n   * **Legality:** Be sure to check your local and state laws first, as about 26 U.S. states outlaw them or require a permit.\n2. **Sugar Glider:** \n   * While they are marsupials rather than rodents, sugar gliders have the same adorable gliding membrane (patagium), big eyes, and pocket-sized appeal. They are widely bred, much easier to find, and legal in the vast majority of jurisdictions.\n3. **Plushies and Merchandise:**\n   * If you just love the aesthetic of the Japanese dwarf flying squirrel, many toy manufacturers and artists sell incredibly realistic and cute plush toys (such as the *Wild Republic Cuddlekins Eco Mini Japanese Dwarf Flying Squirrel*) and custom art on platforms like Etsy and Redbubble.",
